WEBVTT

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.640
I'm not so fundamentally enthusiastic

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.380
Even I will participate in this

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.150
It's been a long time since we went for a drive

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.410
Everyone is excited

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.280
He's coming too

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.820
I may have no chance with him right now

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.560
But I'm definitely going

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:38.600
If you've got a good poker face

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.740
There will be something

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.810
Let's head to the mountains

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.780
We'll just get sunburned at the sea

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.920
Even though it's coat season

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.350
He is completely misunderstanding

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.590
What's going on?

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.560
Being this happy

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:14.430
I'm laughing so hard I might burst

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:22.980
I get choked up when I see his back

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:30.880
In the whirlpool of an endless smile

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.720
Damn...

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.160
That's...I think...

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.400
Oh, it's her, Roosevelt's...

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.170
A ghost?!

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.020
Brrrr, it's cold!

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:03.790
Episode #19
Feelings That Don't Come Across
Brrrr, it's cold!

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.690
Episode #19
Feelings That Don't Come Across
I'm tired.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:06.750
Episode #19
Feelings That Don't Come Across

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.160
Episode #19
Feelings That Don't Come Across
I'm sleepy.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.190
Episode #19
Feelings That Don't Come Across
I'm sorry.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:09.660
I'm sorry.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.230
Where's a taxi?

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.160
I'll take you home.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.030
Well...

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.930
The soup I just had isn't keeping
me warm at all. It's that cold!

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.290
You've got a cold?

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.330
Are you okay?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.940
Funny, our bodies can even catch a cold, huh?

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.380
What are you talking about?

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.010
I meant, like a human body.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:35.780
Look, we get headaches and
stomachaches, right?

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.220
What, really?

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.720
You don't get any of that?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.360
Nope...

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.090
Just like what they say,
"Idiots don't catch colds".

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.460
I still get nauseated whenever
I run out of lemons.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.260
Oh, that I have.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.070
Don't you feel sleepy and
sluggish in the morning?

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.830
I do.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:52.070
Sounds like you have low blood
pressure just like a human.
I do.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.400
Sounds like you have low blood
pressure just like a human.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.410
Oh, guess you're right.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.580
Who knows, maybe you're just being lazy!

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.710
I'm the one who has a cold though.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:03.950
Take care of yourself, okay.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.110
Take some cold medicine.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:06.550
Get some rest, okay.

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:07.850
Here it comes!

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.450
Kate, dash!

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.920
Stop!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.550
Good!

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:13.820
I'll see you guys at school!

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:14.990
Okay, bye!

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:15.790
Later!

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:15.990
Rose, take care!
Later!

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.920
Rose, take care!

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.560
Bye.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.300
See ya.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:21.560
Get rid of that cold before you give it to us.
See ya.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.660
Get rid of that cold before you give it to us.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.800
Okay, see ya.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.970
Bye. Hey, Claire, take me home.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.000
Yeah, yeah...

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.660
One "yeah" is enough.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.640
Hello?

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.540
Is this Kate? It's me, Neil from
the Criminal Affairs Bureau!

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.750
Listen to me very carefully.
Lise...Lise is alive!

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:39.380
What?!

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:39.950
Right now, I'm following the van with Lise in it!
What?!

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.520
Right now, I'm following the van with Lise in it!

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.950
They must be heading to Vivaleo
Pharmaceutical Company!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.250
Kate!
Umm...

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.390
Is there anything you know?

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.820
Pharmaceutical company?

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.390
I don't care what it is,
just tell me anything you know!

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:51.960
That man named Herve that you've
been associating with,

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.800
does he have anything to do with that
pharmaceutical company?

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.830
Lise...Lise is really alive?!

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.730
Oh, damn!

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.100
Kate, I'll call you back!

00:03:59.100 --> 00:03:59.900
Where are you right now?

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:00.100
I'm on the Brooklyn Bridge!
Where are you right now?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:00.740
I'm on the Brooklyn Bridge!

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:00.900
I'm on the Brooklyn Bridge!
Hello? Hello?

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.670
Hello? Hello?

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.310
Excuse me!

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.770
Yes?

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.070
What the hell? What are they trying to do?

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.070
Holy shit!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.160
They've got to be frickin' kidding me!

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.690
Are they all right in there?

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.160
It's completely smashed.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.470
Don't go close to the vehicle!
Please get back to your car, I'm the police!

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.030
Huh? Seriously?

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.300
I don't care, just stay in your car!

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.930
Maybe they're dead.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.480
What the hell is this?

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.450
Hey, I said to get back in your car!

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.550
Lise?!

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.550
Lise!

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.060
L...Lise...

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.700
He got shot!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.770
What's going on?

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.910
Is he okay?!

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:12.710
Hurry up, take cover!

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:12.910
What the hell?!
Hurry up, take cover!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.840
What the hell?!

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.510
Who would've thought the police would
have that much information?

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:18.150
Get Lise.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:18.410
Yes, sir.
Get Lise.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.480
Yes, sir.
Give her the medicine.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.110
I know!

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.140
Lise!

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.390
Another one's been shot!

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.320
It's a girl!

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.490
Looks like something happened.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:32.590
I'm gonna get out now.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:34.460
Huh? You mean right here?

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:37.030
Something happened over there?

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.330
An accident?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.000
The car is turned over.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.270
I've heard that someone's been shot.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.710
Apparently, it was a cop.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.640
What?

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.080
Aren't there any more police officers?

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.880
Man, that cop is dead!

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.110
Didn't they say a girl also got shot?

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.260
Is this your friend?

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.060
Yeah, he was a plumber.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.400
Hmm...

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.500
It was around this time last year

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.340
that he developed the symptoms and died.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.440
I see.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.070
He was leading a normal life,

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:22.380
but one day that was terminated.
It's cruel, isn't it?

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:27.580
His girlfriend had no idea so she
kept on looking for him.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.450
I wonder what she's doing now?

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.150
Before long, there won't be any
more tragedies like this.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.090
Do you think so?

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.850
I'm going to get some sleep. I'm exhausted.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.660
Okay...

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.230
No information has been reported
regarding the owner of the van

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.730
which caused the first accident,
or the identity of the body.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:49.300
It still remains unclear whether
Detective Neil Kasdan,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.270
who was killed in the line of duty,
was hit by the gunshot shot from

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:55.000
the van or was involved in another gunfight.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.840
This way, please!

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.380
How do you even eat that thing?

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.700
Hey...

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.730
It makes my jaw hurt just looking at it.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.100
But it's good.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.430
Really?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.100
Yeah...

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.730
I see.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.600
Did you need something?

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.110
Well, can I sit next to you?

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.740
Sure...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.780
This is the place where I saw
you for the first time.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:35.620
Huh?

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:39.290
We were all called in here for the orientation
right after the enrollment.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.860
Oh, were we?

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:45.730
Yeah, and you were sitting diagonally
to the front of me.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.400
Yeah...

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.730
I remember you were already looking feisty.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:55.440
Don't you think this school is a little too strict?

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.040
You feel that way only at the beginning.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.910
I don't understand that Grace thing or whatever.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.710
Oh, that, yeah, it's so stupid.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:01.810
What's up with their uniforms anyway?

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.310
I know! It's so lame!
What's up with their uniforms anyway?

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.940
That looks cool.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.680
I've never seen it in that color.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.550
Hey, do you know him?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.250
Not at all.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.620
And the next time I saw you after that was at
the welcoming party for the new students.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:20.530
That's right. You were being
asked out by a senior.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.060
You were checking me out from far away, huh?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.900
So you knew?

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.600
Actually, I was thinking that maybe you'd come
over and force me into going out with you,

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.900
but it turned out that you were being
asked out by some other girl.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.470
Oh, yeah, that girl...

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:34.740
I was thinking, "Hurry up and dump that
okay-looking girl and come over here!",

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.340
but you were being all polite to her.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:37.810
Hey, you were watching?

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:40.350
Yeah, that was a little frustrating.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.720
And after that, I couldn't find you.

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:45.620
It was raining like crazy that night.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.990
Right, it sure was!

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:51.090
I was waiting for you by the gate forever.
I was soaking wet.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.160
What? I was waiting for you in
the parking lot, soaking wet!

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.030
No way!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.830
I'm serious!

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.730
Oh, man...

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.170
That's my line!

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:07.070
I thought you were totally dense,
getting caught by a boring girl like her.

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:10.610
But the next day we went out
to a movie, remember?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.080
And we both had a touch of a cold.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.020
Oh, yeah, I remember you nose was red.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.120
Shut up.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.660
I see, that's why you had a cold, huh?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.490
No kidding.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.900
We kept on missing each other like that, but we
just agreed to date for no particular reason.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.330
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.430
Rachel, you know...

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.580
I love you, Rachel.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.450
Luke...

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.320
I've always loved you and I still do.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:57.220
I want to start over with you.
I want to do it right this time.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.490
Luke...

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.160
Rachel...

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.900
I know I said many hurtful things to you,

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.130
and I've always kicked myself for it.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:13.110
I'm sorry for misunderstanding you, Rachel.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.840
I love you.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.470
Luke...

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.580
I'm sorry, but...

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:24.080
I'm sorry.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:26.420
Are you serious?

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:33.020
I can't go out with you anymore.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.930
I'm sorry, Luke.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.660
Rachel...

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.100
I'm sorry.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.340
Rachel!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.820
Claire? Is something wrong?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:08.590
Oh...Everyone has memories
of snowy days, right?

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.660
You mean, like, when you were
a kid or something?

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.490
Yeah...

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:15.230
I guess you would, especially if
you live in New York.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:19.600
If you ever forgot those good
memories about snow,

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.000
I wonder if you'd look at it as just cold?

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:29.840
Oh, I don't know...
But you know, the snow is pretty.

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:35.370
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.150
I didn't realize that.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.790
What's going on? What made you
ask me that question?

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.660
Oh, it's nothing.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.700
I think I'm going to the hospital.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:48.830
To see your brother?

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:49.800
Yeah...

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:50.800
How is he?

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:54.200
It's better than I thought.
He's doing rehabilitation too.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.340
I see.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:57.270
He's one lucky son of a bitch.

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:58.840
You need an umbrella?

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.780
We're not far from the parking lot.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.740
Drive safely, okay.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.810
Yeah...

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:09.250
Those detectives who used to come
talk to you often before...

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:13.150
I've heard that the one of them is missing
and the other one is dead.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.050
I saw that on the news this morning.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:22.430
The situation that you're in has been
worsening little by little every day.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:26.300
The environment you're in is
steadily getting worse.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.070
I can't take this anymore. I've had it!

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:31.710
Paula?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.510
Wow, it's pretty hard.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:33.170
Don't touch that.
Wow, it's pretty hard.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:33.540
Don't touch that.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.780
It doesn't hurt?

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:36.340
It itches.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:37.410
Hmm...

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:41.720
It's like, doing something that I'm not used
to doing makes it even itchier.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:42.780
What's that book?

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:45.520
I've been studying every day.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.060
All kinds of different teachers
come by here every day.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.220
What do you mean by that?

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.960
I'm talking about Pops.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.830
He's been sending those people to me.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.530
Dad did that? Why?

00:13:54.530 --> 00:14:00.330
He admitted that the concept that I came up
with for the business wasn't bad.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.370
What?

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:05.070
But the thing is, I didn't know the
basics of the business,

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.310
so I failed.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.140
Is that why he's been making you study?

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.580
Now, I understand what he's talking about.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:14.570
I was naive, that's for sure.
He's got me thinking.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.450
But he's...

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.220
Claire...

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:17.450
He disappears when you need him the most.
Claire...

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:20.690
He disappears when you need him the most.

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:23.720
Now, he's hooking you up with teachers
instead of money this time, huh?

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:27.360
Claire, I don't look at it that way.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:30.060
The fact that I failed is my own problem.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.830
And that is why I'm going to start over again.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:35.740
I'm going to study from the very beginning
and make it happen this time.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.640
Are you sure you really want to do business?

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:38.970
Of course I do!

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.180
That's why I'm reading a book like this,

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:44.380
and listening to those teachers at my age!

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.410
And that's why Pops is helping me.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.020
See, he hasn't given up on me.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:50.890
Yeah, maybe so, but...

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:56.620
I'm going to make it happen, because
Pops has been this supportive.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.290
I'm going to do this and repay him.

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:01.620
Randy...

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.890
Have you seen him?

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:13.370
Kate, every time you were late for
school or absent from school,

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:16.040
it made me very nervous to tell you the truth.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:20.680
I'm sorry. I've caused Grace so much trouble.

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.310
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.090
It's no big deal for me to cover for you,

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:30.020
or smooth things over between you
and the other members of Grace.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:37.060
What I was afraid of was you getting
severely injured or hurt.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.000
I was afraid of that more than anything
every time you were out of my sight.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.630
Paula?

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:50.110
I'm sorry that I didn't tell you all this time.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.550
What?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.240
I knew about it.

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:55.880
But I don't know what you're talking about...

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:59.090
It's okay, you don't have to hide it.
I know everything.

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:03.790
I know about everything that's happened to you.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.700
What are you talking about?

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.100
This cold hand...

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:14.470
I'd do anything to bring warmth
back into this hand.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.970
But you're already...

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.610
Paula...

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:23.780
It killed me inside, just picturing you
being terrified of the assembly.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.210
No way...

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:29.950
I prayed for your safety every
night after midnight.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.420
I couldn't tell you.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:36.390
I've known about it all along,
but I couldn't tell you.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:39.850
I wanted to help you more.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.950
Paula...

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:47.670
That's why you covered for me so many times.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.430
I'm sorry!

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.210
I'm sorry for not being able to
do anything else for you!

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:56.070
Paula, that's not true! That's not true!

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:01.540
Because of you, I didn't have to deal
with hardships at school.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.580
Because of you, I didn't let it
discourage me along the way.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:11.330
I was scared for a long time,
but you always helped me at school!

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:13.830
Kate...
I was scared for a long time,
but you always helped me at school!

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:18.590
I don't want to lose you.
I don't want you to be like Lise.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.330
Don't go anywhere! Stay by me forever!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.830
Paula...

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:29.770
I love you. I will always love you.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.120
How's it going?

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.740
You sure have hung in there. I'm impressed!

00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:41.390
I just had to do it.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.220
Guess you're right...

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:45.790
But you ignored the union and worked overtime.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.460
I'd appreciate it if you don't sue me, all right.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.830
Thank you so much.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.400
Rose...

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.480
Rose! Rose!

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.440
You wait right there!

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:16.060
I've talked to an insider.

00:18:16.060 --> 00:18:18.860
Lise's condition has manifested, they said.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:23.800
Supposedly, a few researchers
were killed by her after that.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:25.000
Are you sure?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:30.970
Yeah, they said she's sleeping on the bed right
now in the research room, in a human form.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:36.710
Even if they use an Animus' body, the
moment they inject our blood into it,

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.110
the curse will transfer to their bodies.

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:40.980
The experiment was a failure.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:43.350
That's what it sounds like.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.420
Yeah, they could have a new baby,
but that doesn't mean

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.720
they'd never have to worry about
the manifestations again.

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:51.990
They're pathetic...Now, they panic.

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:57.230
They should've saved Mireille before they
conducted an experiment like that.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:01.000
What they have left is only Anna.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.560
Saving Anna is the only way left for them.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.540
I'm sure even they've realized that by now.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.740
We're going to attack the Animus and
obtain the other book of curses!

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.490
Dad...

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:23.790
Don't worry, we're heading to the
hospital now, so sleep some more.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.090
I'm sorry...

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:27.720
Don't worry.

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:38.100
Vivaleo Pharmaceutical...

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.110
Aren't you going to answer?

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:47.110
It's Kate.

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:48.740
What?

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.390
Hello?

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:59.290
I'm in front of the pharmaceutical
company right now.

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:00.760
Oh...

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:04.000
Is Lise alive?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.300
Yes, she is.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:09.270
Then, please, give back Lise.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:09.840
That's impossible.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:10.740
Why? What did Lise do to deserve this?
That's impossible.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.340
Why? What did Lise do to deserve this?

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:15.110
She didn't do anything. I just took her there.

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:15.780
Then!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:16.110
I've already left that place.
I'm not inside that building.
Then!

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.950
I've already left that place.
I'm not inside that building.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.450
There's nothing I can do.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:24.150
Herve, please, I want to see her,
even if just for a little while!

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:26.890
It's pointless. Lise isn't Lise anymore.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:27.820
What do you mean by that?!

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:30.520
I'm hanging up now. Don't call me again.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:34.290
What's that?

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:34.930
Let me go!
Kate?

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:35.300
What's wrong?
Let me go!
Kate?

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:35.660
What's wrong?

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:35.930
What's wrong?
Kate!

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:36.060
Kate!

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:36.660
Did something happen? Hey!
Kate!

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.390
Did something happen? Hey!

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:44.170
It's them. They must've captured Kate.

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:45.370
What?

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:49.710
They've already failed with Lise,
but they're still trying to

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:51.980
continue with the experiment with a new body.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.410
Let's go, Herve!

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.110
Those persistent sons of bitches...

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:31.390
My only love sprung from my only hate

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.790
Too early seen unknown, and known too late

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:38.720
Prodigious birth of love it is to me,
that I must love a loathed enemy

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:41.560
Step by step, I lost track of time

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:44.130
And kept on dancing when I met you

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.430
Without knowing the fate that lies in the stars

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:48.970
I can't stop falling in love

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.540
An unfaithful moon's lacking morals

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:53.870
Give light to my full-on desire

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.240
Grasping onto fate, I scream out

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:58.810
"Wherefore art thou Juliet?"

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.610
Go ahead and laugh at it

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.950
And call it stupid love

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.520
Throw it all

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:07.950
Because I'll be right there

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:11.060
Oh, my Juliet...

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:15.500
Tell me God, what do I do

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:20.730
To make my wishes come true?

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:25.370
Ah! This is so painful

00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:28.210
I howl into the night sky

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:36.350
Does everyone go to sleep

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:39.590
Holding onto a thought like this?

00:22:39.590 --> 00:22:43.890
Ah! Open your eyes right away

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:46.730
Laugh at it if it's a joke

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:49.160
Oh, my sweet Juliet

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:53.270
You who's sleeping and I with no name

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:54.770
Pelted by tragic rain

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.430
Say good die

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:06.340
Two people clash with each other.
True feelings...

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:09.650
The girl of that day is gone.

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:10.950
Episode #20
The Room That's Left Behind
The girl of that day is gone.

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:14.510
Episode #20
The Room That's Left Behind
